      "description": "Watch Leicester vs Northampton highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Carabao Cup returned on August 8, 2026, featuring an intriguing knockout encounter between Leicester City and Northampton Town . Both sides entered the fray with a clear objective: securing a spot in the next round through a display of tactical discipline and competitive spirit. Early Pressure and the Decisive Header Leicester City established their dominance early in the match, although they received an early warning when Harvey Saunders forced a save from Jakub Stolarczyk in the opening minute. The breakthrough arrived in the 15th minute following a period of sustained pressure. A well-delivered corner from Luke Thomas found Caleb Okoli in the box, and the defender made no mistake, powering a header into the bottom left corner from close range. Following the goal, the Foxes continued to dictate the tempo, with Sammy Braybrooke and Luke Thomas both testing the visitor's resolve. Northampton Town remained a threat on the counter-attack, with Jon Guthrie going close with a header from a corner, but the hosts held their narrow advantage as the teams headed into the tunnel at half-time. Second Half Resilience and Late Drama As the second half unfolded, Northampton Town introduced several substitutions to inject fresh energy into their pursuit of an equalizer. Tyrese Fornah came close in the 74th minute, forcing Jakub Stolarczyk into a crucial save to preserve the lead. Leicester also looked to extend their cushion, with Bobby De Cordova-Reid seeing his effort saved by a sharp Zach Jeacock after a clever through ball from Liam Cullen . The closing stages were characterized by high intensity and tactical fouls, leading to yellow cards for Wes Burns and Tom Watson . Despite eight minutes of added time and a late chance for Olabade Aluko , Leicester City managed to navigate the pressure. The final whistle confirmed 